-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pucangan-inscription"><span class="enc-name">Pucangan inscription</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pucangan inscription is a stone inscription of 1041 issued by Airlangga, king of Kahuripan in East Java, in Sanskrit and Old Javanese.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/puducherry-union-territory"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/puducherry-union-territory.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Puducherry (union territory)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Puducherry is a union territory of India formed from the four former French settlements of Pondicherry, Karaikal, Mahé and Yanam, which lie hundreds of kilometres apart.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/puduhepa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/puduhepa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Puduhepa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Puduhepa was a Hittite queen of the 13th century BCE, wife of Hattusili III and the daughter of a priest of Lawazantiya in Kizzuwatna.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/puebla-state"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/puebla-state.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Puebla (state)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Puebla is a state of central Mexico, east of Mexico City, with its capital at the city of Puebla.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/puebla-tlaxcala-valley"><span class="enc-name">Puebla-Tlaxcala Valley</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Puebla-Tlaxcala Valley is a highland basin of central Mexico, east of the volcanoes Popocatépetl and Iztaccíhuatl, shared by the modern states of Puebla and Tlaxcala.</span></a>